=== Q1. Is the resolved step monotone in the accumulator? ===
    a |-> R(a + p, V) for each fixed p, checked over every pair a <= a'.
  U<3,0>, 8 values
            wrapping | not monotone at    84 of   224   first: a=0 <= a'=7, p=1, but R gives 1 > 0
          saturating | not monotone at     0 of   224
     substitute zero | not monotone at    84 of   224   first: a=0 <= a'=7, p=1, but R gives 1 > 0
  U<2,1>, 8 values
            wrapping | not monotone at    84 of   224   first: a=0 <= a'=7/2, p=1/2, but R gives 1/2 > 0
          saturating | not monotone at     0 of   224
     substitute zero | not monotone at    84 of   224   first: a=0 <= a'=7/2, p=1/2, but R gives 1/2 > 0
  U<4,0>, 16 values
            wrapping | not monotone at   680 of  1920   first: a=0 <= a'=15, p=1, but R gives 1 > 0
          saturating | not monotone at     0 of  1920
     substitute zero | not monotone at   680 of  1920   first: a=0 <= a'=15, p=1, but R gives 1 > 0

=== Q2. Post-fixpoint holds; does soundness follow, and under which g? ===
    Point reading   : a datum denotes exactly its own value.
    Absorbing reading: the top denotes [top, infinity), everything else itself.

    accumulator U<3,0> = [Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(4, 1), Fraction(5, 1), Fraction(6, 1), Fraction(7, 1)]
    element     U<2,0> = [Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(3, 1)]

      resolution |  n |   seqs | unsound, point | unsound, absorbing
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
        wrapping |  1 |      4 |              0 |                  0
        wrapping |  2 |     16 |              0 |                  0
        wrapping |  3 |     64 |              4 |                  4
        wrapping |  4 |    256 |             66 |                 66
        wrapping |  5 |   1024 |            512 |                511
                   witness [absorbing] seq=[Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(3, 1)] exact=8 abstract=0

      saturating |  1 |      4 |              0 |                  0
      saturating |  2 |     16 |              0 |                  0
      saturating |  3 |     64 |              4 |                  0
      saturating |  4 |    256 |             66 |                  0
      saturating |  5 |   1024 |            512 |                  0

 substitute zero |  1 |      4 |              0 |                  0
 substitute zero |  2 |     16 |              0 |                  0
 substitute zero |  3 |     64 |              4 |                  4
 substitute zero |  4 |    256 |             66 |                 66
 substitute zero |  5 |   1024 |            512 |                512
                   witness [absorbing] seq=[Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(3, 1)] exact=8 abstract=0

=== Q3. Does the absorbing reading's soundness stay n-independent? ===
    A post-fixpoint argument's whole value is that the trip count never
    enters.  If the failure count under the absorbing reading is zero for
    every n tried, that is the shape holding; if it grows with n, it is not.
        wrapping | n=1:0/4  n=2:0/16  n=3:4/64  n=4:66/256  n=5:511/1024  n=6:2828/4096  n=7:13064/16384  n=8:55085/65536
      saturating | n=1:0/4  n=2:0/16  n=3:0/64  n=4:0/256  n=5:0/1024  n=6:0/4096  n=7:0/16384  n=8:0/65536
 substitute zero | n=1:0/4  n=2:0/16  n=3:4/64  n=4:66/256  n=5:512/1024  n=6:2860/4096  n=7:13332/16384  n=8:56313/65536

